const e="spaf-drama-dance-festival",c=2025,a="Built from the SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus V10 (22 pages), fetched from the organiser's site. The syllabus prints no venue address for classes, no prize money, no points system beyond certificate bands. The syllabus prints single-year classes for Performance Arts Solo; the template buckets groups differently from the printed classes (for example Open is 'above 16' for most items but 'over 18' or '19 and over' for Verse Speaking), so each competition row lists the printed classes and the age text as printed. Creative Writing prose has no separate fee row in the fee table (the poetry fees are printed under the Creative Writing heading). Adjudicator biographies and the advisory committee list are not captured as rules. Sponsor and logo pages carry no rule text. The syllabus is for 2025, so dates, fees and the Gala Concert are past-edition values kept as Variables.",n={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Singapore Performing Arts Festival - Drama & Dance (face to face and online)",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Entries for the 2025 edition close on {{EntryClosingDate}} (Gala Concert early entries on {{GalaEarlyEntryDate}}). Late fees apply after the closing dates.",Notes:["Each entry needs a separate online entry form.","Age is worked out from the year of birth.","Updates are posted on the festival Facebook page: {{FacebookPage}}."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General rules",Items:["The festival is a member of an international federation of festivals. Adjudicators are working performing arts professionals.","For 2025 both face to face and online options were offered. Public Speaking Solo also has a Hybrid option (performance at the venue, adjudicator on Zoom).","Performers may not offer the same piece in more than one class.","Time limits are generous and pieces should be well within them. A shorter piece is not penalised, but marks are deducted if the time limit is exceeded.","Poetry, prose and solo dramatic items no longer need copyright permission. For duologues and group drama, the performer must check copyright.","The organiser can make changes to these regulations with or without notice.","Each performer or guardian agrees to protect the organiser, its affiliates and sponsors from loss or claims caused by a breach of the terms and conditions.","SPAF is a trade mark and may not be used without written permission."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Who can enter",Items:["The festival is for amateurs only. An amateur is a person who does not earn the main part of their income from the discipline entered.","Holders of recognised drama diplomas and degrees may enter only the Open classes.","Age is worked out using the year of birth (for example, born in 2010 counts as 15 years old for 2025).","For group entries, the class is chosen by the oldest group member.","Group sizes: Performance Arts Group at least 8 members, Choral Speaking at least 8 members, Group Acting (Scripted and Devised) at least 3 members, Team Public Speaking 3 speakers.","Impromptu Speaking is face to face only. Video Blog is online only.","Only face to face entries can be considered for the Gala Concert.","The organiser can turn down entries when a class is full."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to register",Items:["All entries are made through the official online entry form. Use a separate form for each entry.","Closing date for all entries (online and face to face) is {{EntryClosingDate}}. Send entries early.","Entries for the Gala Concert must arrive by {{GalaEarlyEntryDate}} to be considered. Early entries get scheduling priority.","Late fees are charged for entries after the closing dates. The organiser can reject late entries.","A PDF copy of the performance piece or script must be uploaded with the entry form. On the event day a copy must be given to the adjudicator's steward before the performance. Failing to do so may lead to disqualification or loss of marks.","Adjudicator copies must be marked with the performer's name, class and number.","A change of own choice material must be emailed to the organiser at least one week before the performance (face to face only). Failing to do so may lead to disqualification or loss of marks.","Online video entries are sent as a YouTube link only, set to 'Unlisted'. Other ways of sending video are not accepted.","Questions go to {{OrganiserContact}}.","If it is hard to get a copy of a piece, contact the organiser."]},{Key:"fees",Title:"Fees",Items:["Fees are in Singapore dollars and are listed per class on the fee schedule, with Online, Face to face and per-member columns.","Group classes add {{MemberFee}}. Example: a 10 member group in a face to face class paying a $47 base fee pays $47 + (10 x $13) = $177.","Each entry may reserve up to 2 observer passes at {{ObserverPassFee}}. More passes can be bought at the same price if available.","Late entries pay a late fee."]},{Key:"dates",Title:"Dates",Items:["Festival day: {{FestivalDate}} (face to face). The Gala Concert is on the same evening.","Online Zoom sessions with the adjudicators: {{OnlineZoomDate}}. Results are announced in the Zoom session.","Creative Writing is submitted by {{CreativeWritingSubmitDate}}.","Workshops and webinars: {{Webinars}}."]},{Key:"venue",Title:"Venue",Items:["Venue: {{Venue}}","Individual classes take place in a classroom that seats about 30. Group classes take place in a recital studio.","Gala Concert: {{GalaConcert}}"]},{Key:"points",Title:"Marking and certificates",Items:["Certificates follow the federation's bands: Participation, Bronze, Bronze Plus, Silver, Silver Plus, Gold and Gold Star.","Gold Star: a superlative performance with effortless technical control and exceptional artistic individuality.","Gold: an impressive performance, technically and artistically, showing sincerity in its interpretation.","Silver Plus: an excellent performance with fluent technical and artistic skills and emerging individuality.","Silver: a convincing performance showing a degree of ability in presentation and interpretation.","Bronze Plus: a competent performance with some artistic awareness or technical ability but needing more vocal or physical expression.","Bronze: a generally secure performance with developing technique but needing artistic development.","Certificate of Participation: an inconsistent performance, limited in communication, needing accuracy or artistic development.","In group entries each member gets a certificate but there is only one group report.","Each performer receives a written report and a festival certificate."]},{Key:"prizes",Title:"Gala Concert",Items:["Gold Star recipients may be invited to perform in the Gala Concert.","Only face to face entries can be considered for the Gala Concert."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Conduct and adjudication",Items:["The adjudicator may withhold any award and may stop any performance. The adjudicators' decisions are final.","It is forbidden to communicate with the adjudicator in any way.","Online video rules: record in a well-lit, quiet space at 1080P or better (most recent phones are enough); place the camera on a stable surface as the adjudicator's eye, with the whole performance in frame.","Record in one continuous take. Any editing within the video leads to disqualification. The recording must be made no more than 6 months before it is submitted.","Judging is on the performance, not the video production."]},{Key:"reporting",Title:"How the day works",Items:["Face to face: each class lasts about an hour. Performers present in a set order, the adjudicator writes a report form for each, and gives the report at the end of the class.","After all performers have presented, the adjudicator comments on the class as a whole in a master class style.","Online: the adjudicator judges the video offline and writes the report, then holds a Zoom master class session where results are announced."]},{Key:"other",Title:"Support and sponsorship",Items:["Running the festival costs over SGD 40,000, covered by entry fees, admission fees to classes and sponsors.","People can support the festival as a sponsor, with a cash contribution, as a volunteer, or by advertising in the e-programme booklet. Contact the festival email for details.","Public admission to classes is mentioned in the support section; the syllabus gives no further details."]}],Documents:[{Title:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus",Url:"https://spaf.sg/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/SPAF-Drama-Syllabus-2025-SG-V10.pdf"}]},s=[{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, pp.7-8, 12, 15-16",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Team and group entries get a certificate for each member but only one group report.","A group entry pays the base fee plus the per-member fee {{MemberFee}}."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Team and group entries get a certificate for each member but only one group report.
- A group entry pays the base fee plus the per-member fee {{MemberFee}}.`}],t=[],o=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Public Speaking Solo","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.10","Sections":{"About":["Classes 1-5: age 8-10, 11-12, 13-14, 15-16, Open (above 16). A Hybrid option, classes 1(H) to 5(H), has the performance at the festival venue with the adjudicator joining by Zoom. If there is a technical problem the performance is recorded and judged later."],"TimeAndFormat":["Class 1: 3 min. Class 2: 4 min. Class 3: 5 min. Class 4: 5 min plus an interview (face to face). Class 5: 7 min plus an interview (face to face)."],"Rules":["Classes 1 and 2: the topic is sent out one month before the closing date. The student chooses the title and the audience and states both at the start of the speech.","Classes 3, 4 and 5: the student chooses the topic and audience and states them at the start of the speech."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Content: clarity, structure, focus, development and knowledge of the subject.","Communication and delivery: posture, eye contact, gesture, use of visual aids.","Language: variety of suitable language structure and vocabulary."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeePublicSpeaking}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Classes 1-5: age 8-10, 11-12, 13-14, 15-16, Open (above 16). A Hybrid option, classes 1(H) to 5(H), has the performance at the festival venue with the adjudicator joining by Zoom. If there is a technical problem the performance is recorded and judged later.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Class 1: 3 min. Class 2: 4 min. Class 3: 5 min. Class 4: 5 min plus an interview (face to face). Class 5: 7 min plus an interview (face to face).\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Classes 1 and 2: the topic is sent out one month before the closing date. The student chooses the title and the audience and states both at the start of the speech.\\n- Classes 3, 4 and 5: the student chooses the topic and audience and states them at the start of the speech.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Content: clarity, structure, focus, development and knowledge of the subject.\\n- Communication and delivery: posture, eye contact, gesture, use of visual aids.\\n- Language: variety of suitable language structure and vocabulary.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeePublicSpeaking}}"},{"Title":"Team Public Speaking","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.11","Sections":{"About":["Classes 3(G) age 13-14, 4(G) age 15-16, 5(G) Open (above 16). Each team has 3 speakers."],"TimeAndFormat":["Class 3(G): speaker 1 1.5 min, speaker 2 (main) 4 min, speaker 3 1.5 min. Class 4(G): 1.5 / 4.5 / 1.5 min. Class 5(G): 1.5 / 5 / 1.5 min. These are maximum limits."],"Rules":["Two topics are set for each class and released one month before the closing date. The team chooses one."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeTeamPublicSpeaking}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Classes 3(G) age 13-14, 4(G) age 15-16, 5(G) Open (above 16). Each team has 3 speakers.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Class 3(G): speaker 1 1.5 min, speaker 2 (main) 4 min, speaker 3 1.5 min. Class 4(G): 1.5 / 4.5 / 1.5 min. Class 5(G): 1.5 / 5 / 1.5 min. These are maximum limits.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Two topics are set for each class and released one month before the closing date. The team chooses one.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeTeamPublicSpeaking}}"},{"Title":"Performance Arts Solo","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.12","Sections":{"About":["A performance can combine some of these skills: storytelling, singing, movement or dance, acting, mime, physical theatre. Props or costumes may be added."],"TimeAndFormat":["Class 6 (age 6): 2 skills, 1-1.5 min. Class 7 (age 7): 2 skills, 1.5-2 min. Class 8 (age 8): 2 skills, 2-2.5 min. Class 9 (age 9): 2 skills, 2.5-3 min. Class 10 (age 10): 3 skills, 3-3.5 min. Class 11 (age 11): 3 skills, 3.5-4 min. Class 12 (age 12): 3 skills, 3.5-4 min. Class 13 Senior (13-16): 4 skills, 4-5 min. Class 14 Open (over 16): 5 skills, 5-6 min."],"Rules":["All performances are memorised and all props are handled by the performer. Prompting, reading text or help from another person is penalised.","All scripts must be submitted. For storytelling, submit the storyboard, because some improvisation is allowed if it improves the performance.","The skills to be assessed must be identified.","Storytelling with props or costumes counts as 2 skills (expressive speaking and props). Storytelling with voice, movement and song counts as 3 skills."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Creativity of presentation, vocal audibility, clarity and expression, inventive use of the body and the space, joining the chosen skills together, and engagement with the audience."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeePerformanceArtsSolo}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A performance can combine some of these skills: storytelling, singing, movement or dance, acting, mime, physical theatre. Props or costumes may be added.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Class 6 (age 6): 2 skills, 1-1.5 min. Class 7 (age 7): 2 skills, 1.5-2 min. Class 8 (age 8): 2 skills, 2-2.5 min. Class 9 (age 9): 2 skills, 2.5-3 min. Class 10 (age 10): 3 skills, 3-3.5 min. Class 11 (age 11): 3 skills, 3.5-4 min. Class 12 (age 12): 3 skills, 3.5-4 min. Class 13 Senior (13-16): 4 skills, 4-5 min. Class 14 Open (over 16): 5 skills, 5-6 min.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- All performances are memorised and all props are handled by the performer. Prompting, reading text or help from another person is penalised.\\n- All scripts must be submitted. For storytelling, submit the storyboard, because some improvisation is allowed if it improves the performance.\\n- The skills to be assessed must be identified.\\n- Storytelling with props or costumes counts as 2 skills (expressive speaking and props). Storytelling with voice, movement and song counts as 3 skills.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Creativity of presentation, vocal audibility, clarity and expression, inventive use of the body and the space, joining the chosen skills together, and engagement with the audience.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeePerformanceArtsSolo}}"},{"Title":"Performance Arts Group","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.12","Sections":{"About":["Classes 6(G) age 6-9, 10(G) age 10-12, 13(G) age 13-16, 14(G) over 16. Minimum 8 members, no maximum."],"TimeAndFormat":["Class 6(G): 2 skills, 3-4 min. Class 10(G): 3 skills, 4-5 min. Class 13(G): 4 skills, 5-6 min. Class 14(G): 5 skills, 6-7 min."],"Rules":["All performances are memorised and all props are handled by the performers. Prompting, reading text or help from another person is penalised.","All scripts must be submitted, with the skills to be assessed identified.","Group classes are chosen by the oldest group member."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Creativity of presentation, vocal audibility, clarity and expression, inventive use of the body and the space, joining the chosen skills together, and engagement with the audience."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeePerformanceArtsGroup}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Classes 6(G) age 6-9, 10(G) age 10-12, 13(G) age 13-16, 14(G) over 16. Minimum 8 members, no maximum.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Class 6(G): 2 skills, 3-4 min. Class 10(G): 3 skills, 4-5 min. Class 13(G): 4 skills, 5-6 min. Class 14(G): 5 skills, 6-7 min.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- All performances are memorised and all props are handled by the performers. Prompting, reading text or help from another person is penalised.\\n- All scripts must be submitted, with the skills to be assessed identified.\\n- Group classes are chosen by the oldest group member.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Creativity of presentation, vocal audibility, clarity and expression, inventive use of the body and the space, joining the chosen skills together, and engagement with the audience.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeePerformanceArtsGroup}}"},{"Title":"Creative Writing","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.13","Sections":{"About":["Class 15 Lower Junior (6-9): own composition of 200-500 words. Class 16 Upper Junior (10-12): 500-800 words. Class 17 Senior (13-16): 800-1,200 words. Class 18 Open (over 16): 1,500-2,500 words."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Submit by {{CreativeWritingSubmitDate}} with a declaration signed by a person other than the performer that it is the performer's own work."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Inventiveness and ownership of the idea, structure and development of the plot and characters, and creative and suitable language that engages readers."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeCreativeWriting}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Class 15 Lower Junior (6-9): own composition of 200-500 words. Class 16 Upper Junior (10-12): 500-800 words. Class 17 Senior (13-16): 800-1,200 words. Class 18 Open (over 16): 1,500-2,500 words.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Submit by {{CreativeWritingSubmitDate}} with a declaration signed by a person other than the performer that it is the performer's own work.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Inventiveness and ownership of the idea, structure and development of the plot and characters, and creative and suitable language that engages readers.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeCreativeWriting}}"},{"Title":"Creative Writing Poetry","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.13","Sections":{"About":["Class 15P Lower Junior (6-9): up to 12 lines in any format. Class 16P Upper Junior (10-12): up to 14 lines. Class 17P Senior (13-16): 16 lines. Class 18P Open (over 16): 20 lines."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Submit by {{CreativeWritingSubmitDate}} with a declaration signed by a person other than the performer that it is the performer's own work."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Inventiveness and ownership of the idea, structure and development, and creative and suitable language that engages readers."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeCreativeWritingPoetry}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Class 15P Lower Junior (6-9): up to 12 lines in any format. Class 16P Upper Junior (10-12): up to 14 lines. Class 17P Senior (13-16): 16 lines. Class 18P Open (over 16): 20 lines.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Submit by {{CreativeWritingSubmitDate}} with a declaration signed by a person other than the performer that it is the performer's own work.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Inventiveness and ownership of the idea, structure and development, and creative and suitable language that engages readers.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeCreativeWritingPoetry}}"},{"Title":"Verse Speaking","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, pp.14 and 22","Sections":{"About":["Class 19 (6-7), 20 (8-9), 21 (10-12), 22 (13-14): one piece from the prescribed list. Class 23 (15-16): two pieces, one from the list and one of own choice, whole programme not over 4 min. Class 24 (17-18): three contrasting own choice poems with spoken links, 5-6 min. Class 25 (Open, 19 and over): at least four thematically linked poems, 6-8 min plus up to 2 min for links."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Poems are spoken from memory. Prompting or reading from text is penalised.","Prescribed list: class 19 - The Storm (Roger McGough) or Seasons (Christina Rossetti). Class 20 - The Yo-yo Man (Ann Logan) or Magic Cat (Peter Dixon). Class 21 - A Small Dragon (Brian Patten) or The Life of Feet (Jenny Joseph). Class 22 - The 3 Little Pigs (Marian Swinger) or Let No One Steal Your Dreams (Paul Cookson). Class 23 - The Witches School of Flying (Marian Swinger) or Funeral Blues (W H Auden).","The list comes from The Works and The Works 3 by Paul Cookson (Macmillan Children's Books)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Vocal audibility, clarity and expression, facial expression for mood and meaning, fitting use of gesture, and keeping a spontaneous quality."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeVerseSpeaking}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Class 19 (6-7), 20 (8-9), 21 (10-12), 22 (13-14): one piece from the prescribed list. Class 23 (15-16): two pieces, one from the list and one of own choice, whole programme not over 4 min. Class 24 (17-18): three contrasting own choice poems with spoken links, 5-6 min. Class 25 (Open, 19 and over): at least four thematically linked poems, 6-8 min plus up to 2 min for links.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Poems are spoken from memory. Prompting or reading from text is penalised.\\n- Prescribed list: class 19 - The Storm (Roger McGough) or Seasons (Christina Rossetti). Class 20 - The Yo-yo Man (Ann Logan) or Magic Cat (Peter Dixon). Class 21 - A Small Dragon (Brian Patten) or The Life of Feet (Jenny Joseph). Class 22 - The 3 Little Pigs (Marian Swinger) or Let No One Steal Your Dreams (Paul Cookson). Class 23 - The Witches School of Flying (Marian Swinger) or Funeral Blues (W H Auden).\\n- The list comes from The Works and The Works 3 by Paul Cookson (Macmillan Children's Books).\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Vocal audibility, clarity and expression, facial expression for mood and meaning, fitting use of gesture, and keeping a spontaneous quality.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeVerseSpeaking}}"},{"Title":"Impromptu Speaking","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.14","Sections":{"About":["Face to face only. Classes 26 (8-10), 27 (11-12), 28 (13-14), 29 (15-16), 30 (Open, over 16). Create and tell a story around an object or topic given by the adjudicator."],"TimeAndFormat":["Class 26: up to 1.5 min. Class 27: 2 min. Class 28: 2.5 min. Class 29: 3 min. Class 30: 3.5 min.","All performers wait together in breakout room 1. One at a time, in order, each goes to breakout room 2 for 2 minutes of preparation, then to the main room to perform."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Inventive content, a believable structure, clear delivery that develops the plot within the time, and awareness of the audience."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeImpromptu}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Face to face only. Classes 26 (8-10), 27 (11-12), 28 (13-14), 29 (15-16), 30 (Open, over 16). Create and tell a story around an object or topic given by the adjudicator.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Class 26: up to 1.5 min. Class 27: 2 min. Class 28: 2.5 min. Class 29: 3 min. Class 30: 3.5 min.\\n- All performers wait together in breakout room 1. One at a time, in order, each goes to breakout room 2 for 2 minutes of preparation, then to the main room to perform.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Inventive content, a believable structure, clear delivery that develops the plot within the time, and awareness of the audience.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeImpromptu}}"},{"Title":"Choral Speaking","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.15","Sections":{"About":["Class 31 (6-8): own choice of one poem, 2-3 min. Class 32 (9-10): two contrasting poems, whole programme up to 5 min. Class 33 (11-12): two contrasting poems, up to 7 min. Class 34 (13-16): two or three contrasting poems, up to 10 min."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["At least 8 members per group. Performances are memorised.","Movements, sounds and gestures may be added. A conductor is not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Teamwork, voice clarity and expression, how well gestures, movement and sound effects fit in, contrast between the texts (classes 32-34), and natural contact with the audience."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeChoral}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Class 31 (6-8): own choice of one poem, 2-3 min. Class 32 (9-10): two contrasting poems, whole programme up to 5 min. Class 33 (11-12): two contrasting poems, up to 7 min. Class 34 (13-16): two or three contrasting poems, up to 10 min.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At least 8 members per group. Performances are memorised.\\n- Movements, sounds and gestures may be added. A conductor is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Teamwork, voice clarity and expression, how well gestures, movement and sound effects fit in, contrast between the texts (classes 32-34), and natural contact with the audience.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeChoral}}"},{"Title":"Dramatic Monologue","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.15","Sections":{"About":["Own choice. Class 35 (10 and under): up to 2 min. Class 36 (11-12): 3 min. Class 37 (13-14): 5 min. Class 38 (15-16): 7 min. Class 39 (Open, over 16): 13 min."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Pieces are performed from memory.","Hand props, costumes and simple scenery may be used. Set-up time is at most 1 minute and striking at most 1 minute (face to face)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Performance, including characterisation and inhabiting the role in voice and body, and use of the space."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeMonologue}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Own choice. Class 35 (10 and under): up to 2 min. Class 36 (11-12): 3 min. Class 37 (13-14): 5 min. Class 38 (15-16): 7 min. Class 39 (Open, over 16): 13 min.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Pieces are performed from memory.\\n- Hand props, costumes and simple scenery may be used. Set-up time is at most 1 minute and striking at most 1 minute (face to face).\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Performance, including characterisation and inhabiting the role in voice and body, and use of the space.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeMonologue}}"},{"Title":"Dramatic Duologue","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.15","Sections":{"About":["Own choice. Class 40 (10 and under): up to 3 min. Class 41 (11-12): 5 min. Class 42 (13-14): 7 min. Class 43 (15-16): 10 min. Class 44 (Open, over 16): 13 min."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Pieces are performed from memory.","Hand props, costumes and simple scenery may be used. Set-up time is at most 1 minute and striking at most 1 minute (face to face).","Teamwork is essential, and the pair should want to share the story with the audience."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Performance, including characterisation and inhabiting the role in voice and body, use of the space, and teamwork."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeDuologue}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Own choice. Class 40 (10 and under): up to 3 min. Class 41 (11-12): 5 min. Class 42 (13-14): 7 min. Class 43 (15-16): 10 min. Class 44 (Open, over 16): 13 min.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Pieces are performed from memory.\\n- Hand props, costumes and simple scenery may be used. Set-up time is at most 1 minute and striking at most 1 minute (face to face).\\n- Teamwork is essential, and the pair should want to share the story with the audience.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Performance, including characterisation and inhabiting the role in voice and body, use of the space, and teamwork.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeDuologue}}"},{"Title":"Group Acting (Scripted)","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.16","Sections":{"About":["Own choice, minimum 3 members. Class 45 (8 and under): 3-10 min. Class 46 (9-10): 4-10 min. Class 47 (11-12): 6-10 min. Class 48 (13-14): 8-12 min. Class 49 (15-16): 10-15 min. Class 50 (Open, over 16): 12-20 min."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Pieces are performed from memory.","Hand props, costumes and simple scenery may be used. Set-up time is at most 1 minute and striking at most 1 minute (face to face).","Teamwork is essential, and the group should want to share the story with the audience."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Performance, including characterisation and inhabiting the role in voice and body, use of the space, and teamwork."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeGroupScripted}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Own choice, minimum 3 members. Class 45 (8 and under): 3-10 min. Class 46 (9-10): 4-10 min. Class 47 (11-12): 6-10 min. Class 48 (13-14): 8-12 min. Class 49 (15-16): 10-15 min. Class 50 (Open, over 16): 12-20 min.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Pieces are performed from memory.\\n- Hand props, costumes and simple scenery may be used. Set-up time is at most 1 minute and striking at most 1 minute (face to face).\\n- Teamwork is essential, and the group should want to share the story with the audience.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Performance, including characterisation and inhabiting the role in voice and body, use of the space, and teamwork.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeGroupScripted}}"},{"Title":"Group Acting (Devised)","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.16","Sections":{"About":["Own choice, minimum 3 members. Class 51 (8 and under): 3-10 min. Class 52 (9-10): 4-10 min. Class 53 (11-12): 6-10 min. Class 54 (13-14): 8-12 min. Class 55 (15-16): 10-15 min. Class 56 (Open, over 16): 12-20 min."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Pieces are performed from memory.","Hand props, costumes and simple scenery may be used. Set-up time is at most 1 minute and striking at most 1 minute (face to face).","Teamwork is essential, and the group should want to share the story with the audience."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Performance, including characterisation and inhabiting the role in voice and body, use of the space, and teamwork."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeGroupDevised}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Own choice, minimum 3 members. Class 51 (8 and under): 3-10 min. Class 52 (9-10): 4-10 min. Class 53 (11-12): 6-10 min. Class 54 (13-14): 8-12 min. Class 55 (15-16): 10-15 min. Class 56 (Open, over 16): 12-20 min.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Pieces are performed from memory.\\n- Hand props, costumes and simple scenery may be used. Set-up time is at most 1 minute and striking at most 1 minute (face to face).\\n- Teamwork is essential, and the group should want to share the story with the audience.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Performance, including characterisation and inhabiting the role in voice and body, use of the space, and teamwork.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeGroupDevised}}"},{"Title":"Video Blog","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, pp.16-17","Sections":{"About":["Online only. Produce news items (true or devised) and present them in a style of your choice. Classes: 57 (6-7), 58 (8-9), 59 (10-12), 60 (13-14), 61 (15-16), 62 (17-18), 63 (Open, all ages)."],"TimeAndFormat":["Class 57: up to 2 min. Class 58: 2.5-3 min. Class 59: 3.5-4 min. Class 60: 4-5 min. Class 61: 4-5.5 min. Class 62: 6-7 min. Class 63: 6-7 min."],"Rules":["It can be one item or more.","Content is planned but not learnt by heart. Reference notes are allowed.","The performer may be seated, standing or moving around.","The video must not be edited. A variety of settings is allowed but it must be one take."],"Allowed":["Costume, props, and audio or video enhancements, but the main judging is on the criteria below."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Performance style, clarity and expression, content and structure, and delivery and sound effects if suitable."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeVlog}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Online only. Produce news items (true or devised) and present them in a style of your choice. Classes: 57 (6-7), 58 (8-9), 59 (10-12), 60 (13-14), 61 (15-16), 62 (17-18), 63 (Open, all ages).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Class 57: up to 2 min. Class 58: 2.5-3 min. Class 59: 3.5-4 min. Class 60: 4-5 min. Class 61: 4-5.5 min. Class 62: 6-7 min. Class 63: 6-7 min.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- It can be one item or more.\\n- Content is planned but not learnt by heart. Reference notes are allowed.\\n- The performer may be seated, standing or moving around.\\n- The video must not be edited. A variety of settings is allowed but it must be one take.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Costume, props, and audio or video enhancements, but the main judging is on the criteria below.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Performance style, clarity and expression, content and structure, and delivery and sound effects if suitable.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeVlog}}"},{"Title":"Jazz Dance Solo","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.17","Sections":{"About":["Modern jazz dance, solo. SPAF Dance aims to build interest in dance and in western jazz dance forms through adjudication and a mini master class.","Classes: 64 (6-7), 65 (8-9), 66 (10-12), 67 (13-14), 68 (15-16), 69 (Open)."],"TimeAndFormat":["Age 6-7: up to 1.5 min. Age 8-9: 1.5-2.5 min. Age 10-12: 2.5-3 min. Age 13-14: 3-3.5 min. Age 15-16: 3.5-4 min. Open (all ages): 4-5 min."],"Rules":["Dress: leotard or T-shirt with leggings, jazz pants or dance shorts. Clothing must not block movement. Hair is fixed away from the face.","Footwear: barefoot, jazz trainers or suitable dance footwear.","Music: with or without a backing track. The music must not distract from the performance.","Choreography: routines by students or teachers are both accepted.","Filming: fixed camera angle no more than 3 metres from the performer, enough light, one continuous take with no zooming or panning, and a safe dance space, preferably a wooden floor."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Understanding of the dance style, technical ability, variety of dynamics, and awareness of the audience."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeJazz}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Modern jazz dance, solo. SPAF Dance aims to build interest in dance and in western jazz dance forms through adjudication and a mini master class.\\n- Classes: 64 (6-7), 65 (8-9), 66 (10-12), 67 (13-14), 68 (15-16), 69 (Open).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Age 6-7: up to 1.5 min. Age 8-9: 1.5-2.5 min. Age 10-12: 2.5-3 min. Age 13-14: 3-3.5 min. Age 15-16: 3.5-4 min. Open (all ages): 4-5 min.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Dress: leotard or T-shirt with leggings, jazz pants or dance shorts. Clothing must not block movement. Hair is fixed away from the face.\\n- Footwear: barefoot, jazz trainers or suitable dance footwear.\\n- Music: with or without a backing track. The music must not distract from the performance.\\n- Choreography: routines by students or teachers are both accepted.\\n- Filming: fixed camera angle no more than 3 metres from the performer, enough light, one continuous take with no zooming or panning, and a safe dance space, preferably a wooden floor.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Understanding of the dance style, technical ability, variety of dynamics, and awareness of the audience.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeJazz}}"},{"Title":"Lyrical Jazz Dance Solo","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.17","Sections":{"About":["Lyrical jazz dance, solo. SPAF Dance aims to build interest in dance and in western jazz dance forms through adjudication and a mini master class.","Classes: 70 (6-7), 71 (8-9), 72 (10-12), 73 (13-14), 74 (15-16), 75 (Open)."],"TimeAndFormat":["Age 6-7: up to 1.5 min. Age 8-9: 1.5-2.5 min. Age 10-12: 2.5-3 min. Age 13-14: 3-3.5 min. Age 15-16: 3.5-4 min. Open (all ages): 4-5 min."],"Rules":["Dress: leotard or T-shirt with leggings, jazz pants or dance shorts. Clothing must not block movement. Hair is fixed away from the face.","Footwear: barefoot, jazz trainers or suitable dance footwear.","Music: with or without a backing track. The music must not distract from the performance.","Choreography: routines by students or teachers are both accepted.","Filming: fixed camera angle no more than 3 metres from the performer, enough light, one continuous take with no zooming or panning, and a safe dance space, preferably a wooden floor."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Understanding of the dance style, technical ability, variety of dynamics, and awareness of the audience."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeLyrical}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Lyrical jazz dance, solo. SPAF Dance aims to build interest in dance and in western jazz dance forms through adjudication and a mini master class.\\n- Classes: 70 (6-7), 71 (8-9), 72 (10-12), 73 (13-14), 74 (15-16), 75 (Open).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Age 6-7: up to 1.5 min. Age 8-9: 1.5-2.5 min. Age 10-12: 2.5-3 min. Age 13-14: 3-3.5 min. Age 15-16: 3.5-4 min. Open (all ages): 4-5 min.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Dress: leotard or T-shirt with leggings, jazz pants or dance shorts. Clothing must not block movement. Hair is fixed away from the face.\\n- Footwear: barefoot, jazz trainers or suitable dance footwear.\\n- Music: with or without a backing track. The music must not distract from the performance.\\n- Choreography: routines by students or teachers are both accepted.\\n- Filming: fixed camera angle no more than 3 metres from the performer, enough light, one continuous take with no zooming or panning, and a safe dance space, preferably a wooden floor.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Understanding of the dance style, technical ability, variety of dynamics, and awareness of the audience.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeLyrical}}"},{"Title":"Contemporary Jazz Dance Solo","Source":"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.17","Sections":{"About":["Contemporary jazz dance, solo. SPAF Dance aims to build interest in dance and in western jazz dance forms through adjudication and a mini master class.","Classes: 76 (6-7), 77 (8-9), 78 (10-12), 79 (13-14), 80 (15-16), 81 (Open)."],"TimeAndFormat":["Age 6-7: up to 1.5 min. Age 8-9: 1.5-2.5 min. Age 10-12: 2.5-3 min. Age 13-14: 3-3.5 min. Age 15-16: 3.5-4 min. Open (all ages): 4-5 min."],"Rules":["Dress: leotard or T-shirt with leggings, jazz pants or dance shorts. Clothing must not block movement. Hair is fixed away from the face.","Footwear: barefoot, jazz trainers or suitable dance footwear.","Music: with or without a backing track. The music must not distract from the performance.","Choreography: routines by students or teachers are both accepted.","Filming: fixed camera angle no more than 3 metres from the performer, enough light, one continuous take with no zooming or panning, and a safe dance space, preferably a wooden floor."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Understanding of the dance style, technical ability, variety of dynamics, and awareness of the audience."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Fees: {{FeeContemporary}}"]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Contemporary jazz dance, solo. SPAF Dance aims to build interest in dance and in western jazz dance forms through adjudication and a mini master class.\\n- Classes: 76 (6-7), 77 (8-9), 78 (10-12), 79 (13-14), 80 (15-16), 81 (Open).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Age 6-7: up to 1.5 min. Age 8-9: 1.5-2.5 min. Age 10-12: 2.5-3 min. Age 13-14: 3-3.5 min. Age 15-16: 3.5-4 min. Open (all ages): 4-5 min.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Dress: leotard or T-shirt with leggings, jazz pants or dance shorts. Clothing must not block movement. Hair is fixed away from the face.\\n- Footwear: barefoot, jazz trainers or suitable dance footwear.\\n- Music: with or without a backing track. The music must not distract from the performance.\\n- Choreography: routines by students or teachers are both accepted.\\n- Filming: fixed camera angle no more than 3 metres from the performer, enough light, one continuous take with no zooming or panning, and a safe dance space, preferably a wooden floor.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Understanding of the dance style, technical ability, variety of dynamics, and awareness of the audience.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Fees: {{FeeContemporary}}"}]`),i=[],r=[{Key:"FeePublicSpeaking",Kind:"fee",Label:"Public Speaking Solo fees (SGD)",Value:"Online / Face to face: class 1 (8-10) $49/$57; classes 2-4 (11-12, 13-14, 15-16) $56/$65; class 5 (Open) $63/$73. Hybrid (face to face venue, remote adjudicator): 1(H) $53; 2(H)-4(H) $61; 5(H) $68.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeTeamPublicSpeaking",Kind:"fee",Label:"Team Public Speaking fees (SGD)",Value:"Online / Face to face, plus per member: classes 3G (13-14) and 4G (15-16) $56/$64 + $13 per member; class 5G (Open) $63/$73 + $13 per member.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeePerformanceArtsSolo",Kind:"fee",Label:"Performance Arts Solo fees (SGD)",Value:"Online / Face to face: classes 6-9 (age 6 to 9) $44/$50; classes 10-13 (age 10, 11, 12, 13-16) $49/$57; class 14 (over 16) $56/$65.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeePerformanceArtsGroup",Kind:"fee",Label:"Performance Arts Group fees (SGD)",Value:"Online / Face to face, plus per member: class 6G (6-9) $44/$50 + $13; 7G (10-12) $49/$57 + $13; 8G (13-16) $49/$57 + $13; 9G (over 16) $56/$65 + $13.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeCreativeWriting",Kind:"fee",Label:"Creative Writing fees (SGD)",Value:"The fee table prints the Creative Writing fees under Poetry: classes 15(P) and 16(P) $86; 17(P) $94; 18 (over 16) $98. The table prints no separate fee row for the prose classes 15-18.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeCreativeWritingPoetry",Kind:"fee",Label:"Creative Writing Poetry fees (SGD)",Value:"Classes 15(P) (6-9) $86; 16(P) (10-12) $86; 17(P) (13-16) $94; 18 (over 16) $98. One fee, online only.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeVerseSpeaking",Kind:"fee",Label:"Verse Speaking fees (SGD)",Value:"Online / Face to face: classes 19-20 (6-7, 8-9) $49/$57; 21-23 (10-12, 13-14, 15-16) $56/$65; 24 (17-18) and 25 (Open) $63/$73.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeImpromptu",Kind:"fee",Label:"Impromptu Speaking fees (SGD)",Value:"Face to face only: classes 26-29 (8-10, 11-12, 13-14, 15-16) $65; class 30 (Open) $73.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeChoral",Kind:"fee",Label:"Choral Speaking fees (SGD)",Value:"Online / Face to face, plus per member $13: classes 31-33 (6-8, 9-10, 11-12) $63/$73; class 34 (13-16) $91/$107.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeMonologue",Kind:"fee",Label:"Dramatic Monologue fees (SGD)",Value:"Online / Face to face: classes 35-36 (10 and under, 11-12) $49/$57; 37-38 (13-14, 15-16) $56/$65; 39 (Open) $63/$73.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeDuologue",Kind:"fee",Label:"Dramatic Duologue fees (SGD)",Value:"Online / Face to face: class 40 (10 and under) $63/$73; 41-42 (11-12, 13-14) $70/$82; 43-44 (15-16, Open) $77/$90.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeGroupScripted",Kind:"fee",Label:"Group Acting (Scripted) fees (SGD)",Value:"Online / Face to face, plus per member $13: classes 45-47 (8 and under, 9-10, 11-12) $56/$65; 48-49 (13-14, 15-16) $59/$73; 50 (Open) $72/$84.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeGroupDevised",Kind:"fee",Label:"Group Acting (Devised) fees (SGD)",Value:"Online / Face to face, plus per member $13: classes 51-53 (8 and under, 9-10, 11-12) $56/$65; 54-55 (13-14, 15-16) $63/$73; 56 (Open) $72/$84.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeVlog",Kind:"fee",Label:"Video Blog fees (SGD)",Value:"Online only: class 57 (6-7) $49; 58-61 (8-9, 10-12, 13-14, 15-16) $56; 62 (17-18) and 63 (Open) $63.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeJazz",Kind:"fee",Label:"Jazz Dance Solo fees (SGD)",Value:"Online: class 64 (6-7) $49; 65-68 (8-9, 10-12, 13-14, 15-16) $56; 69 (Open) $63.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeLyrical",Kind:"fee",Label:"Lyrical Jazz Dance Solo fees (SGD)",Value:"Online: class 70 (6-7) $49; 71-74 (8-9, 10-12, 13-14, 15-16) $56; 75 (Open) $63.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FeeContemporary",Kind:"fee",Label:"Contemporary Jazz Dance Solo fees (SGD)",Value:"Online: class 76 (6-7) $49; 77-80 (8-9, 10-12, 13-14, 15-16) $56; 81 (Open) $63.",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule (pp.19-21)"},{Key:"FestivalDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Festival day (face to face)",Value:"2025-07-26",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.2 and p.6"},{Key:"EntryClosingDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Closing date for all entries (online and face to face)",Value:"2025-05-31",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.6"},{Key:"GalaEarlyEntryDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Early entry date for the Gala Concert",Value:"2025-05-01",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.6"},{Key:"OnlineZoomDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Online Zoom sessions",Value:"2025-08-03",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.7"},{Key:"CreativeWritingSubmitDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Creative Writing submission date",Value:"2025-06-01",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.13"},{Key:"GalaConcert",Kind:"address",Label:"Gala Concert",Value:{Name:"NAFA Studio Theatre",Address:"Saturday 26 July 2025, 7:00 PM",City:"Singapore",MapUrl:"",Directions:"Face to face entries only; early entries get scheduling priority."},Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.6"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Festival venue",Value:{Name:"To be announced",Address:"The syllabus names no class venue; classes are in classrooms that seat about 30 (individual) and a Recital Studio (group).",City:"Singapore",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.7"},{Key:"OrganiserContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Organiser (MS WORKS)",Value:{Name:"MS WORKS, organiser of SPAF",Role:"Festival office",Phone:"+65 9651 3538 (WhatsApp)",WhatsApp:"+65 9651 3538",Email:"spaf@msworks.sg"},Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, page headers"},{Key:"ObserverPassFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Observer pass",Value:"SGD $12 each; each entry may reserve up to 2",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.7"},{Key:"MemberFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Extra fee per group member",Value:"SGD $13 per member for group classes (face to face), added to the base group fee",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, Fees Schedule"},{Key:"Webinars",Kind:"news",Label:"Workshops and webinars printed in the syllabus",Value:[{Date:"2025-03-24",Title:"Info / intro session and new hybrid format",Text:"Monday 24 March 2025, 5:00 pm.",Url:""},{Date:"2025-05-05",Title:"Public Speaking workshop",Text:"Monday 5 May 2025, 5:00 pm.",Url:""}],Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, p.18"},{Key:"FacebookPage",Kind:"link",Label:"Festival Facebook page for updates",Value:"https://www.facebook.com/spaf.sg",Source:"SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus, pp.6, 18"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules, dates, fees, class tables and video rules captured from the organiser's own 2025 syllabus (V10).",SourceType:"Primary - MS WORKS official SPAF 2025 Drama & Dance Syllabus",Source:"https://spaf.sg/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/SPAF-Drama-Syllabus-2025-SG-V10.pdf",Url:"https://spaf.sg/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/SPAF-Drama-Syllabus-2025-SG-V10.pdf"}],m={TemplateKey:e,Year:2025,Note:a,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:s,AgeGroups:t,Competitions:o,CompetitionAgeGroups:i,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{t as AgeGroups,i as CompetitionAgeGroups,o as Competitions,l as Evidence,a as Note,n as Page,s as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,c as Year,m as default};
